    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25KWiJPRkGcgDQT8pc4YUMR)_\n\nFollows #352 (merged). Sia listed three fixes but said \"two buttons\"; I made three.\n\n## What\n- The lint report (`sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun`) has one button per fix, each with the number of entries it would change. A button is a `sp-bibtex-lint:KIND:FILE` Org link, so `RET` runs it.\n- Three commands, one per fix (one `.bib` file, batches of `sp-bibtex-lint-batch-size` = 50, apply/skip/quit per batch, backup before the first write, nothing written without an answer):\n  - `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-order`: fields in the order of `sp-bibtex-field-order`; values untouched.\n  - `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-indent`: every entry laid out by `bibtex-fill-entry`, the `bibtex-mode` standard.\n  - `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors`, three steps:\n    1. names that are not `Last, First` are rewritten\n    2. names one typo away from an author note\n    3. names with the surname of an author note (below)\n  - For steps 2 and 3, per batch: `n` normalises the name in the BibTeX field to the note's name, `l` adds the name as a vulpea alias of the note (the `.bib` is not changed), `e` asks for each name, `s` skips, `q` quits.\n- Surname matches (step 3), a kind of match of its own:\n  - the report lists them in their own section with their own count, so they do not bury the typos\n  - same surname, and given names that fit the note's name by name: `TW Adorno`, `T. W. Adorno` and `Theodor Adorno` fit `Theodor W. Adorno`; `Michael Smith` is not `John Smith`, and `W Adorno` or `Theodor L. Adorno` are not `Theodor W. Adorno`\n  - several notes with the surname: those with as many given names as the BibTeX name are preferred (`TW Adorno` is `Theodor W. Adorno`, not `Tamara Adorno`); if more than one is left (`T Adorno`) the name is ambiguous, listed in its own section with the candidates, and never changed or aliased\n  - a name that is a typo of a note stays a typo match; a name that is a note's name or alias is not flagged\n- Aliases of a note count as known names. `sp-bibtex-lint-convert` (`C-c w b L`) asks which fix to run.\n- Any entry a fix touches is laid out like `bibtex-fill-entry`.\n- Literate doc updated as bullet lists; it tangles to the committed `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n\n## Tests\n- 40 tests (this file and `sp-batch-report`) pass in Emacs 29 with `sp-cache-dir` and `sp-var-dir` defined, including given-name fits, surname matches, ambiguous names, normalise/alias flows and the report sections.\n- The alias write (`vulpea-buffer-alias-add`) is stubbed; not run on a real note or vault, nor in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule. The branch is not prefixed with the PR number, because the session's branch name was fixed.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsguMS2m92TG5VLGt",
